<p class="lead">
  PDF24 Creator is a genuinely capable free Windows application — but it's an installed program, which is exactly the problem on a work laptop that blocks software installs, a shared or public computer, a Mac or Linux machine (PDF24's desktop app is Windows-only), or simply a moment when downloading and installing something feels like more friction than the task deserves.
</p>

<h2>If you want zero install, on any operating system</h2>
<p>
  <a href="/">keptlocal</a> runs entirely in the browser tab you already have open — no download, no install, no OS restriction. It works identically on Windows, macOS, Linux, Chromebooks, and locked-down work machines where IT policy blocks installing new software but doesn't block visiting a website. 46 tools across PDF, image, and utility categories, with no signup required.
</p>

<h2>If you want a one-time install for offline, unlimited use</h2>
<p>
  PDF24 Creator itself remains a solid choice specifically when you want software installed once and available offline indefinitely, on a Windows machine you control and can install software on. Its feature set is broad, and once installed there's no ongoing dependency on an internet connection at all for any of its tools.
</p>

<h2>If you need OCR or PDF-to-Word conversion</h2>
<p>
  PDF24's desktop app and most server-based tools (iLovePDF, Smallpdf) handle OCR and Word/Excel conversion — genuinely heavier operations that browser-only tools don't yet replicate well. If this is a recurring need, keep one of these bookmarked or installed specifically for it.
</p>

