<h2>The practical takeaway</h2>
<p>
  The right choice mostly comes down to whether installing software is actually an option in the moment. On your own Windows machine with time to set something up once, PDF24 Creator is a reasonable, capable, genuinely free choice. On a locked-down work laptop, a shared computer, a Mac, or when you just need something done in the next thirty seconds without a download, a browser-based tool removes the install question entirely — and keptlocal specifically removes the upload question too, for anything that shouldn't leave your device either way.
</p>

